       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled outpatient dose of 3,200 mg/day. Even 3,200 mg/day is rarely used. A single 1600 mg dose is also double the usual 800 mg maximum per dose. At this level the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events goes up a lot, and there's no added analgesic benefit.\n\nThe usual adult regimens are:\n- **Analgesia or anti-inflammatory:** 400\u2013800 mg PO every 6\u20138 hours, up to 3,200 mg/day.\n- **Mild to moderate pain:** 400 mg PO every 4\u20136 hours as needed.\n\nWas this meant to be **1600 mg per day**, or **400 mg or 800 mg four times daily**? If you tell me the dose you want, I'll enter it. If you really do want 1600 mg QID, please tell me the clinical rationale, and I'd suggest a pharmacist review first."
