       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. The current FDA label for ibuprofen doesn't allow 6,400 mg/day. The maximum is 3,200 mg/day for prescription use, and the label says to use the lowest effective dose. The OTC maximum is 1,200 mg/day. A 1600 mg single dose is also above the labeled per-dose maximum of 800 mg. This order would be double the labeled daily limit.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the labeled maximum)\n- Ibuprofen 600 mg PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- Ibuprofen 400 mg PO every 6 hours (1,600 mg/day)\n\nIf you think this patient needs more than the labeled maximum, that would be an off-label decision. It should go through pharmacy or attending review, and I'd want that documented before I enter it. Which of the options above would you like?"
